# All optional. Defaults shown. Who you are, your folders, timezone and integrations live in data/omni.config.json
# (run `npm run setup`, see omni.config.example.json). An env var here still wins over that file.
# OMNI_PORT=4747
# OMNI_HOST=127.0.0.1
# OMNI_BRAIN_DIR=                           overrides the config's workspace folder (default ~/Omni): cwd + context for non-repo channels
# OMNI_CLAUDE_BIN=claude
# OMNI_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# OMNI_CODEX_BIN=                           codex binary (default: PATH, else the one inside the ChatGPT app)
# OMNI_CURSOR_BIN=                          cursor-agent binary (default: found on PATH)
# OMNI_PERMISSION_MODE=bypassPermissions     headless runs cannot answer prompts
# OMNI_MAX_CONCURRENT=4                      turns running at once; warm idle sessions do not count
# OMNI_MAX_CONCURRENT_CODEX=4               Codex turns at once
# OMNI_MAX_CONCURRENT_CURSOR=4              Cursor Agent turns at once
# OMNI_MAX_CONCURRENT_HERMES=4              Hermes runs at once. Hermes also has its own server-side cap
# OMNI_HERMES_URL=                           overrides the config's Hermes URL, like http://100.x.y.z:8642. Unset in both = Hermes off. The Mac must be on the tailnet. The bearer token is the secret HERMES_API_KEY, not an env var.
# OMNI_KEEPALIVE_SECONDS=600                 keep a thread's claude process warm this long after a turn, 0 = close at once
# OMNI_TASK_KEEPALIVE_SECONDS=14400         keep it up this long while the thread's background agents still run
# OMNI_INTERRUPT_GRACE_MS=8000               after Interrupt, kill the process if the turn has not ended by then
# OMNI_DATA_DIR=./data                        runtime state (db, threads, worktrees, browsers), relative to the repo
# OMNI_AUTOMATIONS_DIR=./automations         the automation YAML files, relative to the repo
# OMNI_BROWSER=1                             attach a Playwright MCP per thread
# OMNI_BROWSER_LIVE=1                        Omni runs each channel's Chrome itself, shown live in the thread's Browser panel
# OMNI_CHROME_BIN=                           Chrome to run (default: Google Chrome, else the newest Playwright Chromium)
# OMNI_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=25                      per-file cap for composer attachments
# OMNI_MODS=0                                1 = load the repo's Claude Code mods (mods/omni-progress) into Claude threads with --plugin-dir
# OMNI_SUGGESTIONS=1                         after a turn, Haiku suggests your next reply; 0 = off
# OMNI_TZ=                                  overrides the config's timezone (default: the system's), used by automations
# OMNI_CONFIG=./data/omni.config.json       where the user config lives, relative to the repo
# OMNI_CENTRAL_BRAIN_DIR=                   overrides the config's central brain folder (brain-export)
# OMNI_AUTOMATION_POLL_SECONDS=120           how often event automations (on: in automations/*.yaml) poll GitHub, 15 at least
# OMNI_SECRET_STORE=                       where secret values live: keychain (macOS default), file (data/secrets.json, 0600; default elsewhere) or libsecret (secret-tool)
# OMNI_WEB_DIST=./web/dist                   built Web UI that npm start serves
# Grok Bot webhook. A secret of the same name wins over these. Paste both from the Omni OS requests
# routine (Grok Bot, Routines tab). Leave them commented to leave Grok Bot off. Do not commit a real value.
# GROKBOT_WEBHOOK_URL=                       the routine's URL. Send to Grok Bot posts here.
# GROKBOT_WEBHOOK_AUTH=                      the bare key, or a value that already starts with Bearer. Either form works. Left out of the log.
